<!-- SECTION 4 — Highlights & Features (visual collage)
     7-tile amplifier layout per radius-ii_knowledge_pack.md §2 Best-in-Class Amplifier Matrix.
     Each tile = one competitor blind spot we're claiming in the slim-wafer category.
     Hero tile leads with the 8″ slim wafer (competing / competing DLR / competing stop at 6″).
     Then CCT-on-J-Box, 6 trim accessories, T-Grid kit, Wet Location, EM driver options,
     Plug-n-Play J-Box system. Each tile maps to a specific competitor blind spot. -->
<section class="hf-section" id="highlights" aria-label="Radius SafeZone Highlights and Features">
  <div class="section-inner hf-inner">

    <p class="hf-eyebrow sec-eyebrow">Highlights &amp; Features</p>
    <h2 class="hf-title sec-title">>Performance that won&rsquo;t melt &mdash; in a slim wafer that holds the rating without a tent.</h2>
    <p class="hf-sub">
      UL 263 + ASTM E119 2-hour fire-rated &middot; Wet Location &middot; 4 sizes (3&Prime; / 4&Prime; / 6&Prime; / 8&Prime;) &middot; 90+ CRI TruColor &middot; 5-CCT on the J-Box &middot; CRCU-EM/JBM EMB compatible &middot; T-Grid kits for 4&Prime; + 6&Prime;.
    </p>

    <div class="hf-grid">

      <!-- Hero tile · 2-HOUR FIRE-RATED — the UL 263 + ASTM E119 story -->
      <div class="hf-tile hf-tile-hero hf-tile-grad-1">
        <div class="hf-tile-image">
          <img src="assets/radius-safezone/radius-safezone-6in-hero-1.png"
               alt="LDRS615-RSZ5 Radius SafeZone — 6″ slim wafer recessed downlight tested to UL 263 and ASTM E119 for 2-hour fire resistance, delivering 1,330 lm at 4000K" />
        </div>
        <div class="hf-tile-overlay">
          <div class="hf-tile-tag">&mdash; Hero &middot; 2-Hour Fire-Rated</div>
          <h3>Holds the Rating. Without a Tent.</h3>
          <p>Tested to <strong>UL 263</strong> and <strong>ASTM E119</strong> at independent lab. The aluminum housing <em>is</em> the rated assembly &mdash; no enclosure box, no firebox, no fishing for a tent above the disk. Same fixture, two install conditions (rated + non-rated). One SKU for the whole building, including corridors cited under <strong>IBC &sect; 712</strong> and <strong>NFPA 101 &sect; 8.6.5</strong>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Row of 2 · CCT on J-Box + 6 Trim Accessories -->
      <div class="hf-row-2">
        <div class="hf-tile hf-tile-grad-2">
          <div class="hf-tile-image">
            <img src="assets/radius-safezone/radius-safezone-jbox.png"
                 alt="Radius SafeZone Plug-n-Play J-Box — exploded view showing the 6″ wafer disk + remote driver J-Box with 5-CCTselect dip switch on the J-Box face — set color before the disk locks into the fire-rated penetration" />
          </div>
          <div class="hf-tile-overlay">
            <div class="hf-tile-tag">5-CCT On the J-Box &middot; Rated Ceiling Ergonomics</div>
            <h3>Set the Color Before the Disk Locks the Rating.</h3>
            <p>5-CCTselect dip switch on the <strong>Plug-n-Play J-Box</strong> &mdash; not the disk face. Toggle <strong>2700 / 3000 / 3500 / 4000 / 5000K</strong> at rough-in, then the disk seats into the UL 263 penetration and stays there. No climbing back through a fire-rated membrane to swap CCT post-install.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hf-tile hf-tile-grad-3">
          <div class="hf-tile-image">
            <img src="assets/radius-safezone/radius-safezone-4in-hero-3.png"
                 alt="Radius SafeZone 4-size matrix — 3″, 4″, 6″, and 8″ apertures on one 2-hour UL 263 fire-rated platform — 4 base SKUs (4 sizes · Flat trim only)" />
          </div>
          <div class="hf-tile-overlay">
            <div class="hf-tile-tag">4 Sizes &middot; One Fire-Rated Catalog</div>
            <h3>3&Prime;, 4&Prime;, 6&Prime;, and 8&Prime; &mdash; All Hold the Rating.</h3>
            <p>Four apertures (<strong>3&Prime; / 4&Prime; / 6&Prime; / 8&Prime;</strong>) on one fire-rated platform &mdash; the only slim-wafer category SKU set to extend 2-hour UL 263 + ASTM E119 protection from a 3&Prime; closet to an 8&Prime; corridor without changing fixture families. One spec, one BOM, one rating.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Row of 2 · T-Grid Kit + Wet Location -->
      <div class="hf-row-2">
        <div class="hf-tile hf-tile-grad-4">
          <div class="hf-tile-image">
            <img src="assets/radius-safezone/radius-safezone-4in-hero-1.png"
                 alt="Radius SafeZone T-Grid Installation Kits — drop-ceiling fire-rated install accessory available in 4″ and 6″ (LDRS-4R1/TGK and LDRS-6R1/TGK), lay-in to a 2×2 or 2×4 grid without cutting tile" />
          </div>
          <div class="hf-tile-overlay">
            <div class="hf-tile-tag">T-Grid Kits &middot; 4&Prime; + 6&Prime;</div>
            <h3>Drop-Ceiling Install Without Cutting Tile.</h3>
            <p>2 catalog-listed T-Grid kits — <code>LDRS-4R1/TGK</code> (4&Prime;) + <code>LDRS-6R1/TGK</code> (6&Prime;) — lay-in to <strong>2&times;2 or 2&times;4 drop-grid</strong> without cutting tile. Carries the 2-hour rating into commercial drop-ceiling corridors where fire-rated assemblies meet T-bar grid.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hf-tile hf-tile-grad-5">
          <div class="hf-tile-image">
            <img src="assets/radius-safezone/radius-safezone-6in-hero-3.png"
                 alt="Radius SafeZone Wet + Fire combo — all 4 base SKUs (4 sizes · Flat trim) ship Wet Location rated AND 2-hour fire-resistant per UL 263 + ASTM E119" />
          </div>
          <div class="hf-tile-overlay">
            <div class="hf-tile-tag">Wet + Fire Combo &middot; All 4 SKUs</div>
            <h3>The Only Slim Wafer That&rsquo;s Both.</h3>
            <p>Most fire-rated downlights ship <em>Dry-only</em>. All 8 SafeZone SKUs (4 sizes &times; 2 trims) are <strong>Wet Location</strong> AND <strong>2-hour fire-resistant</strong> &mdash; the only slim-wafer combo in the category. One SKU lights fire-rated bath/shower assemblies, sprinklered stairwells, exterior soffits, and parking-deck egress.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Row of 2 · EM Driver options + Plug-n-Play J-Box system -->
      <div class="hf-row-2">
        <div class="hf-tile hf-tile-grad-6">
          <div class="hf-tile-image">
            <img src="assets/radius-safezone/radius-safezone-4in-hero-2.png"
                 alt="Radius SafeZone EM Ready — constⒶNT CRCU-EM/JBM 15W Universal-Mount emergency driver + EM15 / JBM datasheet accessories — UL 924, 90-minute runtime, code-compliant egress lighting in 2-hour rated penetrations" />
          </div>
          <div class="hf-tile-overlay">
            <div class="hf-tile-tag">EM Ready &middot; CRCU-EM/JBM + EM15 / JBM</div>
            <h3>Egress Lighting in a Rated Assembly.</h3>
            <p>Pair the SafeZone with <strong>EM15</strong> (all sizes) or <strong>JBM</strong> (6&Prime; + 8&Prime; only per datasheet), plus const<span class="aa" aria-hidden="true">Ⓐ</span>NT <strong>CRCU-EM/JBM</strong> &mdash; 15W EM driver in a universal-mount J-Box. &ge;90 min reduced-lumens egress per <strong>UL&nbsp;924 / NFPA&nbsp;101 &sect;&nbsp;7.9 / IBC &sect;&nbsp;1008.3</strong>. Code-cited egress in a 2-hour rated penetration.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hf-tile hf-tile-grad-2 hf-tile-controls">
          <div class="hf-tile-image">
            <img src="assets/radius-safezone/radius-safezone-6in-hero-2.png"
                 alt="Radius SafeZone Plug-n-Play J-Box system — plenum-rated quick-connect cable from disk to J-Box, electronically isolated junction, integrated aluminum rated housing that holds UL 263 + ASTM E119 without an enclosure box" />
          </div>
          <div class="hf-tile-overlay">
            <div class="hf-tile-tag">Plug-n-Play J-Box &middot; Rated Assembly</div>
            <h3>Disk + J-Box = One Rated Assembly.</h3>
            <p>The <strong>aluminum housing IS the rated assembly</strong> &mdash; no enclosure box, no tent, no firebox. Plenum-rated quick-connect cable from disk to remote J-Box. Drop the disk into the cutout, mount the J-Box behind, both pass <strong>UL 263 + ASTM E119</strong> together. Saves ~30 min/fixture vs. building a fire-rated enclosure around a standard can.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
