      <h2 class="tac-title sec-title">>Three components. <em>Together they hold the rating.</em></h2>
      <p class="tac-desc">
        When you drop a SafeZone into a fire-rated ceiling, you&rsquo;re installing a <strong>rated assembly</strong> &mdash; not just a fixture. <strong>Wafer disk</strong> (spring-clip cutout install) &middot; <strong>Plug-n-Play J-Box</strong> (remote &middot; 5-CCT dip on the face) &middot; optional <strong>T-Grid Installation Kit</strong> (4&Prime; / 6&Prime; &middot; lay-in to 2&times;2 or 2&times;4 grid without cutting tile). Click each component to see what it does and why it matters under <strong>UL 263</strong> and <strong>ASTM E119</strong>.
      </p>

      <!-- 3-tab callout — Install Component Selector.
