        </div>
        <div class="tac-callout-body" id="tacCalloutBody">
          <!-- Component-specific copy. Default = Disk. Updated by JS on tab click. -->
          <p id="tacCalloutCopy">The Radius SafeZone wafer disk &mdash; a stamped aluminum heat-sink with frosted polycarbonate lens, edge-lit PMMA optic, and spring-loaded retention clips. Drops into a standard cutout (3-9/16&Prime; for 3&Prime; &middot; 4-3/4&Prime; for 4&Prime; &middot; 6-13/16&Prime; for 6&Prime; &middot; 8-7/8&Prime; for 8&Prime;) and pops in with the clips. No can, no separate housing, no enclosure box. The aluminum housing has been independently tested as part of the rated assembly to <strong>UL 263</strong> and <strong>ASTM E119</strong> &mdash; meaning the disk + J-Box hold 2-hour fire resistance together with no tent above. A plenum-rated quick-connector cable links the wafer to the remote J-Box (Component 2).</p>
